 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"CurrentStateAggregation-ParentFirmPatterns">Parent Firm Patte=
rns</h1>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 82.1696%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 35.2465%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 31.0821%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 33.6792%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"col" style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" c=
lass=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><strong>Parent =E2=86=92 Child</=
strong></span></p></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Parent =E2=86=92 Child, cr=
oss-Parent</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong style=3D"text-alig=
n: left;">Child =E2=86=92 Child with Parent Grouping (N:N)</strong></th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"400" style=3D"wid=
th:400px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"dcefee80b3bbe4d20bcbaa3ab795a6dc6df78bcff=
10396c21ce485c62fc43f11" height=3D"250"></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"400" style=3D"wid=
th:400px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"82b33413766f59c56da11a27bf5dd5dbb5e3e9737=
3e98d220d4c7fe0864093b0" height=3D"200"></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"400" style=3D"wid=
th:400px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"067f7d8f78b091f0b8611a493560d34a12de2faf0=
e2185f66e10055f8d98aba3" height=3D"84"></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <ul>
           <li data-uuid=3D"cc7359f7-1433-4511-9e2e-55b14e511cc1">Parent ge=
nerally oversees and provides some level of Head Office support - this is d=
one at varying levels of aggregation and maturity</li>
           <li data-uuid=3D"8ec05a3e-9ebc-48f7-a28c-30e2382be4cf">Parent st=
aff typically not sub-organized into child-firm specific divisions, those r=
emain within the child firms, especially in the case of a M&amp;A where reg=
istered firms continue to somewhat operate independently</li>
           <li data-uuid=3D"09200537-439d-498f-9df4-2f5040eed5cb">Child fir=
ms can be registered together (i.e. 1 registration to represent 2 different=
 firm environments) or separately registered</li>
          </ul>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"89642310-8f92-4a8c-b87d-bba96e243d69">In rare ca=
ses a parent acquires another parent (majority interest only for Guardian =
=E2=86=92 R&amp;L) and retains their separate entities</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"a4988a42-1126-4d53-b5c9-fb7279bac9ef">In this pa=
rticular example, until such time as a transition is triggered, the relatio=
nship is more defined as a partnership (e.g. Guardian products, R&amp;L cli=
ent relations) and will look like a delegation use case on the platform</li=
>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"10db216e-d5ba-4989-91a3-badef3d3659c">Parent is =
virtually represented by NBIN to enable firm grouping, and may also be indi=
cated by "Co-mingled IFM" in Firm360 :question:&nbsp; Is this consistent?&n=
bsp; Baskin appears to not be the case</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"06214d2b-a34f-48e0-a1c3-abd7e1e98c54">Users can =
still exist at the "parent-level", where leadership is represented in both =
registered firms</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"CurrentStateAggregation-ParentFirmUserJourney:AccessManagemen=
t">Parent Firm User Journey: Access Management</h1>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 98.6729%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 8.19142%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 20.9057%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 23.6197%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 22.9159%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 24.3732%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Parent Firm Setup =E2=86=92</p></th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Cross-Firm User Access Provisioning =E2=86=92</p></th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Ongoing Management &amp; Attestations =E2=86=92</p></th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>User Offboarding</p></th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Activities</p></th>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"5b49dbae-e238-4d1a-8151-92fd2f98f97b">
           <p>For new firm onboarding, Firm Implementations team works with=
 Data Team to create firm record</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"3e7781d7-dd39-49ee-a3d3-33206b3c1e90">
           <p>For a change in structure. firm notifies NBIN via RVP/Service=
 Team&nbsp;:question:&nbsp;who then submits a request for Firm360 records t=
o be updated</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"bb363a06-75da-4b60-b12b-9712adf1e620">
           <p>Firm Implementations / Support separately processes initial u=
ser setups once the firm is available on CX</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"10deebdb-c034-458a-91a1-04708c49b855">
           <p>Firm-specific subscriptions are elected on Firm360 then enabl=
ed in respective systems</p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"d028cc00-6f38-4486-8cda-90445d71802b">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Access requests are created to=
 one of the child firms</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"0aa0e2e4-1489-47a3-8b94-e084baafeddd">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">NBIN ID User Admin Team proces=
ses the request across CX, R2, SZ and NetRep</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"c014f84e-67ce-4718-9a25-c2259f5e418a">
           <p>FSS completes regular user access reviews to ensure users at =
the firm continue to have the right accesses</p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"da32c10c-e582-417a-8bd9-d7aa5b0bad21">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">FSS completes deactivation req=
uest against the child firm for that user</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>User Interactions</p></th>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <p title=3D"">N/A</p></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li>
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Firm security steward (FSS) su=
bmits a new/change request depending on the child firm used:</span></p>
           <ul>
            <li data-uuid=3D"303f41ed-8899-44b4-8d19-e2697abad296">
             <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">R2&nbsp; + UAF for IB firm a=
ccess</span></p></li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"ba1f95bd-c5d9-4604-9a32-128254f46f7f">
             <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">R2 myRequest for PM &amp; IF=
M</span></p></li>
           </ul></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"ebf54916-d195-43a3-8bc5-fe3b36b0b9b6">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">FSS includes RR ranges of othe=
r child firms for cross-firm access into legacy systems</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"dcc6a9b9-5a81-4c4f-ae80-198679660dad">
           <p>:question: How do PM's request "sub-advisor" cross-firm acces=
s - does R2 form have any RR validations?&nbsp; Does ID Admin run into erro=
rs when trying to assign RR outside of broker code?</p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"f5f71c9f-996f-458e-af68-41779495333d">
           <p><span>Annual R2, SZ, NetRep user attestation reports are gene=
rated by NBIN and delivered per child firm, for FSS to review and act on</s=
pan></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"43bcb675-8a35-423b-a6fa-be47bce68b64">
           <p><span>IB's have self-serve access to R2 user admin portal for=
 ongoing user management</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e6fcff confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e6fcff">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li>
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">FSS submits a delete user acce=
ss request</span></p>
           <ul>
            <li data-uuid=3D"7a37205e-4802-4e07-9341-48b231b4be14">
             <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">For IB, use R2 + UAF</span><=
/p></li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"9b75019f-4404-42e3-b644-615d24da6ed1">
             <p>PM &amp; IFM firm access, use R2 MyRequest</p></li>
           </ul></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"a21c2633-27e1-468d-a285-6c22b5449ec3">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">NBIN ID User Admin team comple=
tes user deactivation in CX (and R2, SZ, NetRep, if required)</span></p></l=
i>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>User Pain Points</p></th>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <p title=3D"">N/A - this step has no firm interactions</p></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"cd112737-230c-4cff-8258-a9a497e5ea25">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Two completely separate proces=
ses to remember when parent has both IB and PM business</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"c65eeb86-33a6-45b2-a504-d0fa985d36e5">
           <p>Parent users have to choose which child firm their ID is crea=
ted under for legacy systems (not intuitive)</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"22404c00-bab0-45ae-b0d6-bf0c2c69bcd5">
           <p>In R2, RR ranges outside of the firm's broker code cannot be =
used (NetRep / SZ :question: does not have this limitation)</p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"b031f267-131f-42e8-afa0-d1da7133f14b">
           <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;color:#333333;">No holis=
tic, auditable view of parent firm user access; reliance on institutional k=
nowledge</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"7e6c2f78-369e-474b-b04d-a8aee447d07a">
           <p>Annual user attestation reports are generated per child firm;=
 FSS must manually reconcile reports to identify parent firm users.</p></li=
>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"63ea070d-1c92-4e0a-a7e3-ea1f1b7c54ac">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">FSS has to remember to deactiv=
ate or delete the user in each child firm via tool or request</span></p></l=
i>
          <li data-uuid=3D"523c14d7-36d3-4bd0-ae7d-d28be11f9e8a">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Separated, inconsistent access=
 request workflows by child firm type.</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d6a49afd-5a38-4975-a928-2af02ee0104a">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">High risk of incomplete offboa=
rding, leading to security&nbsp;</span>exposure</p></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Business Frictions</p></th>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"27d46e57-696e-4e3c-b607-9f140be369f1">
           <p>Firm360 setup and platform setup are distinct and separate st=
eps</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"de8133d4-eeda-446e-997a-97ba735cdc6a">
           <p>:question: For add-on features by license, it is unclear whic=
h child firm / user&nbsp;gets allocated the license</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"7c643b84-9a81-479c-9264-243a236ceef9">Core packa=
ge for different firm types may conflict&nbsp;</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d65e6f7e-05fb-4bad-9183-a348025231d3">Firm360 so=
metimes has errors</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"f9f1ac63-fc45-4873-8e4a-fd4c861e9f12">
           <p>Firm relationship is invisible to access admin - :question: m=
ay run into errors when requesting cross-firm access outside of broker code=
 in R2</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"cc6ad0ea-b9a8-4a7f-a227-5a74038bf66c">
           <p>Setup of single user may result in processing 2 or more reque=
sts</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"95a38906-d9cf-483c-be19-8354afec80cb">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">User access updates are proces=
sed differently across each platform, leading to RR discrepancies across ID=
's&nbsp;</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"414bd568-a107-4da4-8860-73333c6da489">
           <p>Risk of privacy breach - unclear and difficult to audit acces=
s assignments</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"c93badaf-05d7-4caa-867c-93e96ba55991">
           <p>Inability of catching inconsistent entitlements across firms<=
/p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"93bdf7aa-9dba-4619-8f54-741ebae7743e">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">High risk of incomplete offboa=
rding, leading to security exposure</span></p></li>
          <li>
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Unable to connect the multiple=
 ids of a given user and streamlining the user deactivation.</span></p></li=
>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Opportunities</p></th>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e3fcef">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"e2fffb08-2fbf-4fa3-9891-7d3671c220c4">
           <p>Enable firm hierarchy in CX to align with Firm360</p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e3fcef">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li>
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Harmonize cross-firm provision=
ing rules across platforms</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"abfb308f-973d-4454-88d4-205765e7d8ad">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Enable single ID to grant acce=
ss to multiple firms</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"477c2757-ec74-4fbc-85d7-85be4114f1f6">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">Streamline request flow betwee=
n firm types</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"3edaf77f-7941-4ce4-81e9-ee4c266ac4c4">Clarify de=
cision path for user on which firm / level is the setup</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e3fcef">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"a9135acc-df6f-486a-a03f-1d9403aac84f">
           <p>Appropriately signal which users belong to which firm to simp=
lify user identification and cross-firm RR auditability</p></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e3fcef">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li>
           <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">&nbsp;ID lineage and synchroni=
zation</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Constraints &amp; Considerations</p></th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d56176c8-f11a-4814-bceb-f76665ae196f">Future fea=
tures may only be available at parent level e.g. custody fee, firm analytic=
s</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"2c689724-49df-49d2-9664-c551914b9a3d">:question:=
 Explore potential conflicts between firm access vs. NBIN firm billing</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">&nbsp;</span></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><br></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#333333;">&nbsp;</span></p></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <h1 id=3D"CurrentStateAggregation-FeatureRelationship"><span style=3D"f=
ont-size: 24.0px;letter-spacing: -0.01em;">Feature Relationship</span></h1>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"7d825c11-1103-458b-9129-e5962be26435"><span>Contracts=
 are established at the registered firm-level for billing</span></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"dc616d14-011a-424a-b745-810d13ebb73b"><span>There are=
 different ways for features to be billed,&nbsp;</span></li>
    </ul>
